# PostgreSQL Conventions

## General

- Use PostgreSQL 18 via Docker
- Connection via `NUXT_DATABASE_URL` environment variable, bound to `runtimeConfig.databaseUrl`. Server code reads `useRuntimeConfig().databaseUrl`; standalone tools (`tools/seed.mjs`, `tools/migrate.mjs`) read `process.env.NUXT_DATABASE_URL` directly because they run outside the Nitro runtime.
- LISTEN/NOTIFY available for realtime if needed

## Naming

- Table names: plural, snake_case (`users`, `order_items`)
- Column names: snake_case (`created_at`, `user_id`)
- Primary keys: `id`
- Foreign keys: `<referenced_table_singular>_id` (`user_id`, `order_id`)
- Indexes: `idx_<table>_<columns>` (`idx_users_email`)
- Timestamps: `created_at`, `updated_at`

## Data Types

- Use `uuid` for primary keys (with `gen_random_uuid()`)
- Use `text` over `varchar` (PostgreSQL treats them the same)
- Use `timestamp` for dates (not `date` unless date-only is needed)
- Use `boolean` for true/false values
- Use `jsonb` for structured data (not `json`)
- Use `serial` only for auto-incrementing counters

## Security

- Never expose database credentials in client-side code
- Use parameterized queries (Drizzle handles this automatically)
- Never expose tables directly; always use server API routes
